# Isaac Sim / Isaac Lab runtime output
# `artifacts/*` and not `artifacts/`, because git cannot re-include anything
# under an excluded *directory* -- the negation below only works if what is
# excluded is the directory's contents.
artifacts/*
# ...except the campaign scripts. They are 108 KB of shell that encodes which
# arms were run, in what order and why -- the reasoning behind every number in
# evidence/, and the only record of it. Ignoring them meant a clone got the
# results and none of the design, and the handoff's references resolved to
# nothing. The outputs beside them stay ignored.
!artifacts/campaign/
artifacts/campaign/*
!artifacts/campaign/*.sh
benchmarks/*.json
outputs/
logs/
checkpoints/
datasets/
videos/
wandb/
runs/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.hdf5
*.mp4

# Local machine state
environment-lock.local.json
*.local.ps1

# Per-machine coding-agent settings; the shared CLAUDE.md is tracked, this is not.
.claude/settings.local.json
